    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d911">

                <pb facs="1021" n="877" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg877"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.44 Sun Yat Sen/39: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-22T16:00:00-04:00">May 22, 1929—4
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>169. …</p>
                <p>Referring to your 384, May 14, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="92" xml:id="d911-f1"/> Navy
                    Department desires that Commander in Chief U. S. Asiatic Fleet participate
                    officially in the ceremonies and the Secretary of the Navy informs me he has
                    instructed <pb facs="1022" n="878" xml:id="pg878"/> the Commander in Chief to
                    attend the ceremonies as a member of your special mission and to communicate
                    with you regarding details.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
